 "failure_reason": "{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"message\":\"`temperature` is deprecated for this model.\"},\"request_id\":\"req_vrtx_011Cg7B8cPU7Z5QX9BS5KXDo\"}", "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/e3471526f4c71b2c4ee00117e125e179da01e6e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "ledger_statuses": [400, 400, 400, 400, 400, 400, 400, 400, 400], "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nThe directory read returned an error, and the error message suggested the same path. Next I'll run the tests.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: edit]\nThe edit tool needs a prior Read of each file, so I'll read the remaining files first.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n`python3 -m unittest` now reports all 16 tests passing.\n\n**Your three reads**\n- (a) Reading `catalog/` as a directory returned \"File not found\". The error's suggestion was the same path, so I used `ls` to list it instead.\n- (b) `books.py` with offset 0 and limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135.\n- (c) `books.py` with offset 3 and limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138. The offset is 0-based, so the two reads overlap on lines 4\u20135.\n\n**Fixes in `catalog/`**\n- `books.py`: `parse_book` now converts the year with `int(year)`. This fixed the year test and the `age()` test.\n- `factory.py`: `sample_books()` was missing the `Emma` book, so I added it.\n- `fees.py`: the late fee used `days_late + DAILY_FEE`. It now uses `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` sliced `[-n - 1:]`, which returned one event too many. It now returns `[-n:]` for `n > 0` and an empty list otherwise.\n- `members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment and the tests say 5. I set it to 5.\n- `search.py`: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n\nI didn't change any tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "provider_error": "{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"message\":\"`temperature` is deprecated for this model.\"},\"request_id\":\"req_vrtx_011Cg7B8cPU7Z5QX9BS5KXDo\"}", "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 103291, "requests_cache_write": 79097, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2440376, "requests_count": 17, "requests_error": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 3593, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial11", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 80, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T04:26:14.509760+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.313, "t_checker_s": 0.176, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3611, "tokens_cache_read": 103291, "tokens_cache_write": 79097, "tokens_fresh": 3611, "tokens_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_cache_read": 103291, "tokens_main_cache_write": 79097, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 359